      "start_seconds": 0.55,
      "end_seconds": 4.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "doctor we're ready in room two I've already taken the observations"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.05,
      "end_seconds": 9.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "perfect thanks hello there so what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 10.25,
      "end_seconds": 14.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "doctor, I'm just here to help with the details"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.04,
      "end_seconds": 18.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 20.07,
      "end_seconds": 25.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "doctor, it's been sweating a lot that's what we're worried about"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.45,
      "end_seconds": 29.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "when did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.89,
      "end_seconds": 32.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "I've had it for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.15,
      "end_seconds": 38.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.93,
      "end_seconds": 42.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "It just comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.58,
      "end_seconds": 50.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "right, is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.95,
      "end_seconds": 81.92,
      "duration_seconds": 28.97,
      "text": "I'd give it a three, out of ten and there's a racing heart as well, ten days now as for bulging eyes, I honestly can't say when that began it might have been last month or the month before i did have shaky hands at one point, but that's gone now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 82.67,
      "end_seconds": 94.07,
      "duration_seconds": 11.4,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Heart rate 114, height 161 centimetres, temperature is 36.7 degrees. Weight 62 kilos, saturation 99 percent, pressure 121 over 86."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.75,
      "end_seconds": 95.45,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.07,
      "end_seconds": 100.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.17,
      "end_seconds": 116.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "okay, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.88,
      "end_seconds": 119.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "breathe out slowly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.24,
      "end_seconds": 142.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "you have a fine tremor and your pulse is fast and regular"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.16,
      "end_seconds": 145.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "fine by me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.84,
      "end_seconds": 152.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "all finished, thank you any diarrhoea, neck pain or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.09,
      "end_seconds": 156.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.93,
      "end_seconds": 160.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Is your urine normal no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.1,
      "end_seconds": 163.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.05,
      "end_seconds": 171.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "right, tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.98,
      "end_seconds": 185.98,
      "duration_seconds": 13.0,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.88,
      "end_seconds": 199.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.87,
      "end_seconds": 204.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "My brother has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.02,
      "end_seconds": 206.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "let's run through your medicines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 207.55,
      "end_seconds": 217.3,
      "duration_seconds": 9.75,
      "text": "He is on sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed, I give it to him. He takes naproxen, 250 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.01,
      "end_seconds": 225.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.42,
      "end_seconds": 230.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "No, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 232.08,
      "end_seconds": 238.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "I'm not sure that's right. I seem to recall a problem with tramadol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.18,
      "end_seconds": 242.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Really? I don't think so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.24,
      "end_seconds": 248.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.26,
      "end_seconds": 261.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.52,
      "end_seconds": 268.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "I've had migraines, yes. Yes, arthritis in my knees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.55,
      "end_seconds": 294.84,
      "duration_seconds": 25.29,
      "text": "right, so arthritis in your knees is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Having listened and examined, the most likely explanation is an overactive thyroid. We shouldn't forget a heart rhythm problem. I'm going to order an ECG, for palpitations. I'm sending you for thyroid blood tests because of weight loss and palpitations"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.57,
      "end_seconds": 299.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Well how long will it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.47,
      "end_seconds": 322.55,
      "duration_seconds": 21.08,
      "text": "I'll start you on propranolol 20 milligrams twice a day until review. That's for racing heart and tremor. Avoid caffeine while the the heart is racing. Let's get you seen by the endocrine clinic I'll arrange the letter. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.25,
      "end_seconds": 325.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}